\section{The equation and the trivial family}

We consider
\begin{equation}\label{eq:main}
y^{2}=(36n^{3}-19-12mn)^{2}-(2m)^{3},\qquad(n,m,y)\in\mathbb{Z}^{3}.
\end{equation}
Setting $m=0$ gives the \emph{trivial family} $y=\pm(36n^{3}-19)$.
Throughout, \emph{solution} means a triple with $m\neq0$; since only $y^{2}$
appears, solutions come in signed pairs $(n,m,\pm|y|)$ and we list triples
$(n,m,|y|)$.

